🔹 Problem

👉 Given:

array nums
integer k

👉 Find maximum average of any subarray of size k

🔹 Example
nums = [1,12,-5,-6,50,3]
k = 4

Subarrays of size 4:

[1,12,-5,-6] → sum = 2 → avg = 0.5
[12,-5,-6,50] → sum = 51 → avg = 12.75 ✅
[-5,-6,50,3] → sum = 42 → avg = 10.5

👉 Answer = 12.75

🔴 1. BRUTE FORCE

👉 Har subarray ke liye sum calculate karo

🔹 Code (basic)
double findMaxAverage(vector<int>& nums, int k) {
    int n = nums.size();
    double maxAvg = -1e9;

    for (int i = 0; i <= n - k; i++) {
        int sum = 0;

        for (int j = i; j < i + k; j++) {
            sum += nums[j];
        }

        double avg = (double)sum / k;
        maxAvg = max(maxAvg, avg);
    }

    return maxAvg;
}
🔹 Complexity
Time = O(n * k) ❌


🟢 2. OPTIMAL (Sliding Window)

👉 Window size fixed = k
👉 Har step:

ek element add
ek remove

double findMaxAverage(vector<int>& nums, int k) {
    int n = nums.size();

    // first window sum
    int sum = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {
        sum += nums[i];
    }

    int maxSum = sum;

    // sliding window
    for (int i = k; i < n; i++) {
        sum += nums[i];       // add new
        sum -= nums[i - k];   // remove old

        maxSum = max(maxSum, sum);
    }

    return (double)maxSum / k;

🔥 Dry Run (Visualization)

nums = [1,12,-5,-6,50,3], k=4

Step 1: First window
[1, 12, -5, -6] → sum = 2
Slide 1:
remove 1, add 50
[12, -5, -6, 50] → sum = 51 ✅
Slide 2:
remove 12, add 3
[-5, -6, 50, 3] → sum = 42

👉 Max sum = 51
👉 Max avg = 51 / 4 = 12.75

🔥 Complexity
Time = O(n) ✅
Space = O(1)
🧠 Important Insight

👉 Average maximize karna = sum maximize karna
👉 Isliye directly sum track karo (shortcut logic)
